"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"d0cfabbc89f73c6fe28857aff1727bae7b3447d2","date":"2026-09-09T21:12:09-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#799)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"949ad19f6abe33f84a56f623690821c95068628c","date":"2026-09-09T17:59:20-04:00","message":"(fix) Form engine shouldn't create global CSS rules (#798)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"ad9786412cd423a86c54f889b4e87cf6cf59d61e","date":"2026-09-09T12:53:22-04:00","message":"(fix) Reduce re-render churn in FormProcessorFactory (#670)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Re-write some core hooks in the form-processor-factory to reduce churn\n\nIn the FormProcessorFactory, there's serious potential for render\ncascades from the combinations of `useEffect()` and `setState()` that\nthen trigger additional `useEffect()` and `setState()` calls. This\ncommit switches to more aggressively caching some of these key hooks so\nthat there's less potential for these cascade to lead to catastrophic\nreloading issues.\n\n* Reduce churn in processor context\n\nThis is basically done by splitting the processor context into a \"static\"\npart that is derived from the form itself and a \"dynamic\" part that may\nbe updated by components downstream of the FormProcessorFactory. This\nmostly should optimize things so that components that depend on the\nprocessor context should mostly get stable objects, assuming they\ncorrectly use the properties of the processor.","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"954cee04af4f957d9cea4f57137a63d5a793d021","date":"2026-09-09T09:26:06-04:00","message":"(feat) Wrap FormEngine in Suspense boundary (#797)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"9246d19d3fe662ccc060a800854110