026-06-18T06:20:21-04:00","message":"(chore) Release patch version (#758)","refs":"tag: v4.2.1","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"523127afc5f604aac9efe19c9bbd59927bace803","date":"2026-06-18T01:23:52-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#757)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"12c24b6731b62e0993ae8ecbe666b13785f71f6e","date":"2026-06-12T12:11:44+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5735: Only send default encounter datetimes for stopped visits","refs":"","body":"PR #756 made new encounters always submit an explicit encounterDatetime,\nfalling back to the client-clock session date. On browsers running ahead\nof server time this produces a future datetime that the backend rejects\nwith Encounter.datetimeShouldBeBeforeCurrent, breaking form submissions\nin active visits (caught by patient-chart's clock-skew e2e test).\n\nRestore the previous behavior for active visits and visit-less encounters:\nomit encounterDatetime so the backend defaults it to server time. Keep\nsending the visit-window-clamped session date for stopped visits, which\nis the retrospective data entry case O3-5735 fixed.\n","authorName":"denniskigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b99cb4c27946bf936dce89d37baebe31720f8ef8","date":"2026-06-11T23:02:01+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5735: Keep default encounter datetimes within the visit window during retrospective data entry (#756)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"4b5b8e1262ec464906a9f3e8e060035ce3bd9ea8","date":"2026-06-09T11:18:52-04:00","message":"(chore) Release version 4.2.0 (#755)","refs":"tag: v4.2.0","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"22996e79c501d39d557361e9dd2c98e410ebcc46","date":"2026-06-09T17:23:34+05:30","message":"(chore) Bump @openmrs/esm-framework peer dependency to 10.x (#754)","r