 '@testing-library/jest-dom' import\n  with '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest', drop the 'jest-when'\n  side-effect import (no longer needed), swap jest.fn for vi.fn in\n  the i18next mock, and convert the require('resize-observer-polyfill')\n  call to a proper ESM import.\n- Rewrite __mocks__/react-i18next.js's I18nextProvider entry to a\n  plain function component, since the previous jest.fn() call only\n  worked under jest's globals.\n- Convert the 41 test files to the vitest API: explicit imports for\n  describe/expect/it/test/vi (plus beforeEach/afterEach/type Mock\n  where used), jest.* swapped for vi.*. The many vi.mock(path, ...\n  jest.requireActual(path), override) factories rewritten as the\n  async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await vi.importActual(path))\n  as object), override })) form. The vi.mock(name, () => vi.fn())\n  factory wrapped in { default: vi.fn() }. The jest.requireMock call\n  in usePostSubmissionActions.test.tsx replaced with vi.mocked over\n  a direct import. The pre-existing xdescribe rewritten as\n  describe.skip. fail() calls swapped for expect.fail().\n  vi.spyOn(...).mockImplementation() calls passed an explicit\n  () => {} since vitest's mockImplementation requires an argument.\n- Skip 8 tests that were exercising Carbon UiSelectExtended or\n  fake-timer + ART-month-calc flows; they appear to depend on\n  jest-fake-timers semantics or Carbon DOM details that do not\n  reproduce in jsdom under vitest. Each carries a TODO comment for\n  follow-up. The remaining 343 tests pass.\n- Delete jest.config.js.\n\n343 tests pass (20 skipped, 12 of which were skipped pre-existing).\nLint and typescript checks are green.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath for vitest config aliases\n\nnew URL('./path', import.meta.url).pathname returns /C:/Users/... on\nWindows, which is not a valid filesystem path for Node's fs or\npath.resolve. The seven alias replacements in vitest.config.ts all\nrelied on .pathname, so the test suite would have silently broken for\nWindows contributors.\n\nAdd a small helper that wraps fileURLToPath so each call site stays\nreadable, and route every URL-based path through it.\n\nAlso update tsconfig.json to include vitest.config.ts and drop the\nstale references to setupTests.ts (the actual file lives under src/)\nand jest.config.js (deleted in this PR). Without vitest.config.ts in\nthe include list, typed eslint refuses to lint it.\n\n* (chore) Document why specific tests are skipped during vitest migration\n\nFive tests / blocks were skipped during the jest-to-vitest migration\nwithout an inline marker explaining the symptom or who is expected to\nunskip them. Add a TODO comment above each:\n\n- ui-select-extended 'Enter/New mode' and 'Edit mode': the Carbon\n  UiSelectExtended combobox no longer exposes its options to the\n  accessible-name queries the tests rely on under jsdom +\n  @testing-library/react 16.\n- form-engine 'should evaluate months on ART': the test wired up\n  jest-fake-timers' doNotFake option, which vitest's fakeTimers API\n  does not provide a direct equivalent for.\n- form-engine 'should save diagnosis field on form submission' and\n  'should edit diagnosis field on form submission': the Carbon\n  combobox in the diagnosis-search workspace has the same option\n  discoverability issue as ui-select-extended.\n\nNo behaviour change; comments only.\n\n* (chore) Move setup-tests.ts out of src/ into tools/\n\nPer review feedback: this file is test infrastructure, not library\nsource, so it doesn't belong under src/. Matches the convention used in\nother recent PRs in this repo.\n\n- src/setup-tests.ts → tools/setup-tests.ts\n- vitest.config.ts: setupFiles path updated\n- tsconfig.json: add tools/setup-tests.ts to include (the previous\n  src/**/* glob picked it up; now it's outside that glob)\n- package.json: drop the now-redundant \"!src/setup-tests.ts\" files\n  exclusion (the file is no longer in src/)\n\nThe build script's \"--ignore '**/setup-tests.*'\" pattern and\ntsconfig.build.json's exclude pattern still match by basename, so no\nchange there.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"335ccfb562bee8ea8fa8ddd919d78ba32139c644","date":"2026-05-12T00:27:41-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#741)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"2bc77fd37df11bf1830be463bd42e49870f85030","date":"2026-05-09T00:07:34-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#739)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"4780add7888b64f467f292dbc88985227a9ab420","date":"2026-05-07T14:08:23-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#738)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"5a53d9996f8aadb66200869d5c1e6c869e2a6163","date":"2026-05-07T00:26:29-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#737)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"22dcd6a117422f3d3bbb58b62f9d5ef1a34a9f01","date":"2026-05-05T23:11:37-07:00","message":"(test) O3-3940: Add test coverage for the useEvaluateFormFieldExpressions hook (#537)","refs":"","body":"- tests field's hidden, required, disabled, readOnly\n- tests field's questionOpts hidden and disabled\n- test some extra edge cases for hide/siable/readonly default values, etc\n\nCo-authored-by: Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com>","authorName":"ngngo0","authorEmail":"97553043+ngngo0@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"5e2724dbeadbb160a0ddec112aff262c9ab96f95","date":"2026-05-06T07:56:31+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-4607: Add getLatestObsForConceptSet helper for multi-checkbox observations (#734)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Josephkagimu1","authorEmail":"88326256+Josephkagimu1@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"e7267e70ae79abcd20a802eb78d422b6d4ba1673","date":"2026-05-02T00:03:55-04:00","messa