{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WB2jqtqvo2AS4NmukHnk7Y","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"ebb02b719931d121419669b531b6e05c77f515e9","date":"2026-10-02T21:57:25+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions\n\nHide logic only kept hidden top-level obs out of the encounter payload.\nHidden obs group members, test orders and diagnoses kept whatever value\nwas entered before the field was hidden, so they were still submitted\neven though the form no longer showed them.\n\nprocessObsGroup now skips hidden members and, in edit mode, voids their\nstored obs, the same way top-level obs are handled. It reads each\nmember's visibility and stored obs from the flattened form field,\nbecause hide evaluation and hydration update that copy rather than the\none held in the group's questions. prepareOrders and prepareDiagnosis\nnow skip hidden fields.\n\n* Evaluate hide logic for repeated field instances\n\nRows added to a repeating field kept their hidden state from when they\nwere created, so hiding a repeating test order, diagnosis or obs group\nmember left its extra rows in the encounter payload. Extra group rows\nalso stayed visible in the form.\n\nfindFieldSection looks up the field's page through meta.pageId, which\nrepeated instances don't carry because cloneRepeatField replaces their\nmeta. Reading sections off the missing page threw inside the\nfieldDependents loop in handleFieldLogic, so none of the repeated\ninstances had their hide expression re-evaluated. It now returns\nundefined when the page isn't found, which skips the section visibility\nupdate for repeated instances since they aren't in the form schema.\n\n* (fix) Preserve pending deletions for hidden orders and diagnoses\n\nFiltering hidden fields out of encounter submissions discarded explicit deletions when a previously cleared field became hidden. Keep pending voided values for hidden orders and diagnoses while excluding their new values. Leave stored values untouched when no deletion is pending, and preserve existing submission behavior for visible fields.\n\n* Skip deleted repeated rows when evaluating field dependents\n\nDeleting a repeated row removes it from formFields but leaves its id in\nthe fieldDependents of any field its hide expression references. The\nnext change to that field made evaluateFieldDependents read\nquestionOptions off undefined, which threw and stopped the remaining\ndependents, including other repeated rows, from being re-hidden.\n\nevaluateFieldDependents now skips dependent ids that are no longer in\nformFields.\n\n* Keep the stored uuid of nested obs groups\n\nprocessObsGroup recursed into nested groups with the copy held in the\nparent group's questions, which hydration doesn't reach. When a member\nof a nested group was hidden and nothing else in that group was edited,\nthe nested group went out without its stored uuid, so the backend\nwould treat it as a new group rather than update the existing one.\n\nThe type check, the recursion and the submission reads now use the\nflattened form field, the same copy already used for the hidden check.\nhasSubmittableObs also reuses isFieldHidden instead of repeating the\ncheck.\n\n* Leave hidden swapped orders and diagnoses as they are\n\nA swap sets voidedValue alongside newValue, so keeping only voidedValue\nfor a hidden order turned a replacement into a plain delete: the stored\norder was voided and nothing replaced it. A hidden diagnosis swapped\ndirectly was left alone, so the two behaved differently.\n\nHidden orders and diagnoses now only submit their voided value when\nthere's no newValue, which means the field was explicitly cleared.\nSwapped and reanswered values are left as they are.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"12c24b6731b62e0993ae8ecbe666b13785f71f6e","date":"2026-06-12T12:11:44+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5735: Only send default encounter datetimes for stopped visits","refs":"","body":"PR #756 made new encounters always submit an explicit encounterDatetime,\nfalling back to the client-clock session date. On browsers running ahead\nof server time this produces a future datetime that the backend rejects\nwith Encounter.datetimeShouldBeBeforeCurrent, breaking form submissions\nin active visits (caught by patient-chart's clock-skew e2e test).\n\nRestore the previous behavior for active visits and visit-less encounters:\nomit encounterDatetime so the backend defaults it to server time. Keep\nsending the visit-window-clamped session date for stopped visits, which\nis the retrospective data entry case O3-5735 fixed.\n","authorName":"denniskigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b99cb4c27946bf936dce89d37baebe31720f8ef8","date":"2026-06-11T23:02:01+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5735: Keep default encounter datetimes within the visit window during retrospective data entry (#756)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":3}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e747080a-6a4d-4bdc-8efe-c5babb2c8c48","uuid":"f5a50daf-4f5e-404d-948d-315a21cea7fa","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:59:02.893Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"ebb02b719931d121419669b531b6e05c77f515e9","date":"2026-10-02T21:57:25+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions\n\nHide logic only kept hidden top-level obs out of the encounter payload.\nHidden obs group members, test orders and diagnoses kept whatever value\nwas entered before the field was hidden, so they were still submitted\neven though the form no longer showed them.\n\nprocessObsGroup now skips hidden members and, in edit mode, voids their\nstored obs, the same way top-level obs are handled. It reads each\nmember's visibility and stored obs from the flattened form field,\nbecause hide evaluation and hydration update that copy rather than the\none held in the group's questions. prepareOrders and prepareDiagnosis\nnow skip hidden fields.\n\n* Evaluate hide logic for repeated field instances\n\nRows added to a repeating field kept their hidden state from when they\nwere created, so hiding a repeating test order, diagnosis or obs group\nmember left its extra rows in the encounter payload. Extra group rows\nalso stayed visible in the form.\n\nfindFieldSection looks up the field's page through meta.pageId, which\nrepeated instances don't carry because cloneRepeatField replaces their\nmeta. Reading sections off the missing page threw inside the\nfieldDependents loop in handleFieldLogic, so none of the repeated\ninstances had their hide expression re-evaluated. It now returns\nundefined when the page isn't found, which skips the section visibility\nupdate for repeated instances since they aren't in the form schema.\n\n* (fix) Preserve pending deletions for hidden orders and diagnoses\n\nFiltering hidden fields out of encounter submissions discarded explicit deletions when a previously cleared field became hidden. Keep pending voided values for hidden orders and diagnoses while excluding their new values. Leave stored values untouched when no deletion is pending, and preserve existing submission behavior for visible fields.\n\n* Skip deleted repeated rows when evaluating field dependents\n\nDeleting a repeated row removes it from formFields but leaves its id in\nthe fieldDependents of any field its hide expression references. The\nnext change to that field made evaluateFieldDependents read\nquestionOptions off undefined, which threw and stopped the remaining\ndependents, including other repeated rows, from being re-hidden.\n\nevaluateFieldDependents now skips dependent ids that are no longer in\nformFields.\n\n* Keep the stored uuid of nested obs groups\n\nprocessObsGroup recursed into nested groups with the copy held in the\nparent group's questions, which hydration doesn't reach. When a member\nof a nested group was hidden and nothing else in that group was edited,\nthe nested group went out without its stored uuid, so the backend\nwould treat it as a new group rather than update the existing one.\n\nThe type check, the recursion and the submission reads now use the\nflattened form field, the same copy already used for the hidden check.\nhasSubmittableObs also reuses isFieldHidden instead of repeating the\ncheck.\n\n* Leave hidden swapped orders and diagnoses as they are\n\nA swap sets voidedValue alongside newValue, so keeping only voidedValue\nfor a hidden order turned a replacement into a plain delete: the stored\norder was voided and nothing replaced it. A hidden diagnosis swapped\ndirectly was left alone, so the two behaved differently.\n\nHidden orders and diagnoses now only submit their voided value when\nthere's no newValue, which means the field was explicitly cleared.\nSwapped and reanswered values are left as they are.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"12c24b6731b62e0993ae8ecbe666b13785f71f6e","date":"2026-06-12T12:11:44+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5735: Only send default encounter datetimes for stopped visits","refs":"","body":"PR #756 made new encounters always submit an explicit encounterDatetime,\nfalling back to the client-clock session date. On browsers running ahead\nof server time this produces a future datetime that the backend rejects\nwith Encounter.datetimeShouldBeBeforeCurrent, breaking form submissions\nin active visits (caught by patient-chart's clock-skew e2e test).\n\nRestore the previous behavior for active visits and visit-less encounters:\nomit encounterDatetime so the backend defaults it to server time. Keep\nsending the visit-window-clamped session date for stopped visits, which\nis the retrospective data entry case O3-5735 fixed.\n","authorName":"denniskigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b99cb4c27946bf936dce89d37baebe31720f8ef8","date":"2026-06-11T23:02:01+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5735: Keep default encounter datetimes within the visit window during retrospective data entry (#756)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":3}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WB2jqtqvo2AS4NmukHnk7Y","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
